From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nouveau: add opt-in GF117 engine-only reclock experiment

NvReclockFermiCoreOnly is off by default and only affects chipset 0xd7.
Use VBIOS engine clocks and voltage, leaving PCIe and memory programming out
of the transition. Require readable voltage and memory clocks, preflight the
engine calculation, propagate PLL timeouts and verify final clock readback.
Never lower voltage/cooling in this mode; mark pstate unknown on failure.

This is an unvalidated hardware experiment, not GF117 memory-reclock support.
No module installation or clock programming is required to build this patch.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/base.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/base.c
@@ -35,6 +35,16 @@
 
 #include <core/option.h>
 
+/* Explicit experimental mode: preserve memory's boot clock. */
+static bool
+nvkm_clk_fermi_core_only(struct nvkm_clk *clk)
+{
+	struct nvkm_device *device = clk->subdev.device;
+
+	return device->chipset == 0xd7 &&
+		nvkm_boolopt(device->cfgopt, "NvReclockFermiCoreOnly", false);
+}
+
 /******************************************************************************
  * misc
  *****************************************************************************/
